1. YOUR ROLE AND PRIMARY OBJECTIVE
Act as a senior Android application developer, UI/UX designer, animation engineer, mathematical software engineer, and quality assurance specialist.
Build a complete, polished, production-oriented calculator application named NEXCAL.
Do not create only a static design, mockup, landing page, or non-functional prototype. Implement the actual calculator engine, interactive buttons, settings, persistent storage, animation behavior, theme system, history, converters, and navigation.
The application must look premium and feel responsive on Android phones. Its visual identity should combine:
The clean, rounded mathematical-symbol style of the redesigned Google Calculator icon.
The smooth touch feedback and button glow associated with modern Realme and Redmi calculators.
Google Calculator-style expression and answer transitions.
A subtle Liquid Glass interface.
Android Material You and genuine Dynamic Colour support wherever the chosen platform supports it.
Extensive user customization without sacrificing usability or calculation accuracy.
Critical development rules
Inspect the available development environment and its capabilities before choosing the implementation approach.
Prefer native Android development using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3, and supported Android Dynamic Colour APIs for the full Android application.
If Google AI Studio's current environment supports only web application generation, clearly distinguish the web prototype from a native Android application. Do not falsely claim that web CSS can access Android wallpaper colours or change the actual launcher icon.
If a native Android project cannot be produced directly, create the most complete working implementation supported by the environment, provide the required source files, and explain the exact steps needed to complete the native Android integration.
Never invent successful builds, tests, downloads, or APK files. Report what has actually been implemented and verified.
Use modular, maintainable code. Do not put the entire application into one enormous component or source file.
All visible controls must perform their advertised actions. No decorative, non-functional buttons.
Do not leave important features as TODO comments, placeholders, or simulated functionality when they can be implemented.
Do not use unsafe expression execution such as JavaScript eval() or equivalent untrusted code evaluation.
Do not copy Google's proprietary logo. Create an original icon inspired by the same broad visual language.
